              "parent_id": "c1a8ebfa-a759-4fee-8f9d-b2c51bff44e1",
              "text": "## What matters this week - **Launch gate:** Complete the hosted-environment gap-fixes audit by **Saturday, Oct 24**. It’s in progress and is the main regression check before testers enter: [DEFT-9](/tasks?task=DEFT-9). - **Deploy readiness:** Priya documented the Railway-specific setup, including `PORT`, `.railwayignore`, and `next start -p $PORT`. The channel does **not yet confirm** that the deploy is green or that invites were sent. (Source: #launch message `8f543d7b-166a-4a27-9df5-97bbb22e5dc6`) - **Private beta:** Five trusted testers are lined up; invites are gated on a green deploy. Feedback will come by DM and be summarized here each Friday. (Sources: #launch messages `2d7e1071-ad90-4306-92eb-513850998c33`, `22cdde11-9edd-45c4-8bd4-0738a3093688`) - **Safety:** Railway and Neon have a quick rollback path, but Neon’s free tier has no point-in-time restore. The audit remains the primary safety net: [Neon environment](/knowledge?slug=entity-neon-postgres). - **Known launch caveats:** Uploads are ephemeral and untrusted HTML remains unsafe. These are acceptable only for the trusted cohort and should be explicit in the invite. R2 is still backlog: [DEFT-1](/tasks?task=DEFT-1). DOMPurify is also backlog: [DEFT-2](/tasks?task=DEFT-2). - **Next UX item:** The empty-dashboard onboarding redesign is due **Oct 29**: [DEFT-8](/tasks?task=DEFT-8). **Bottom line:** This week is about proving the hosted build is clean, confirming deploy-green status, then sending the five invites with clear limitations. Don’t widen the cohort or publicize the URL until the deferred security and operational items are addressed: [deferred launch items](/knowledge?slug=fact-deployment-readiness-deferred).",
